The fix for this specific bug is the same as before — check the Preview box for that variable. The more useful lesson is the diagnostic reflex it should trigger: **when a bug reproduces on preview and nowhere else (or production and nowhere else), check environment variables before assuming it's a code problem.** A quick way to confirm the hypothesis without guessing:

```tsx
// temporary, removed after diagnosing — never ships
export async function POST(req: Request) {
  if (!process.env.PDF_SERVICE_KEY) {
    return new Response('PDF_SERVICE_KEY missing in this environment', { status: 500 });
  }
  // ...
}
```

A clear, specific error like that (instead of a generic 500) turns a confusing "works on my machine" bug report into a two-minute fix: check the dashboard, check the box, redeploy. The habit worth building is checking this *before* diving into the feature's own logic, since a same-code-different-environment bug is, by definition, not a logic bug at all.
